1
00:00:03,159 --> 00:00:13,219
Add users and control what they can see — Settings ▸ Access Control — Two gates decide what a person sees: the plan you are on, and the role you gave them.

2
00:00:18,553 --> 00:00:31,801
Settings ▸ User Management is everyone with a sign-in, and the role each of them carries.

3
00:00:31,801 --> 00:00:40,819
A new user needs a name, a work email and a role — the role is the part that decides what they see.

4
00:00:40,819 --> 00:00:55,938
Give the narrowest role that still lets them do the job. Widening one later is easy; unwinding an over-wide one is not.

5
00:00:55,938 --> 00:01:05,777
They sign in with that once and set their own — you are not the keeper of anybody’s password.

6
00:01:05,777 --> 00:01:13,036
Roles & Permissions is the whole matrix on one screen: View, Create, Edit, Delete, per module.

7
00:01:13,036 --> 00:01:18,074
Admin is protected — it always keeps everything, so you can never lock yourself out.

8
00:01:18,074 --> 00:01:26,516
A doctor can view and create claims but not delete them. Staff never reach Settings or Backup at all.

9
00:01:26,516 --> 00:01:33,213
Accounting and Inventory go finer still: per resource, and with approve and export as their own permissions.

10
00:01:33,213 --> 00:01:44,278
That is how a billing manager can approve a payable while nobody else can — and why exports are worth guarding.

11
00:01:44,278 --> 00:01:50,553
There is a second gate: your plan. Modules outside it are hidden from everyone, whatever their role.

12
00:01:50,553 --> 00:01:57,678
So "why can’t I see this" has exactly two answers — the plan does not include it, or the role does not allow it.

13
00:01:58,050 --> 00:02:15,470
What you just did

14
00:02:16,331 --> 00:02:25,331
